    <statement><p>You live in Grid-Town on the corner of 2nd and 4th, and work in a building on the corner of 20th and 16th. How many routes are there which take you from home to work and then back home, but by a different route?</p>
<p><fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\mathop{\rm C}\nolimits\mathopen{}\left(30,18\right)\mathopen{}\left(\mathop{\rm C}\nolimits\mathopen{}\left(30,18\right)-1\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p><m>{30 \choose 18}\left({30 \choose 18} - 1\right)</m> routes.  For each of the <m>\binom{30}{18}</m> routes to work, there is exactly one less route back.</p>
</solution>
